<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carnatic Sultanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1692–1855</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Arcot State</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carnatic Sultanate was a state in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> ruled by the Nawabs of the Carnatic, or of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcot">Arcot</a>, from about 1692 to 1855. First Mughal governors, the nawabs became independent rulers but were drawn into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnatic-wars">Carnatic Wars</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and fell under British control. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> took over their lands in 1801 and abolished the title in 1855.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carnatic-sultanate.jpg" alt="Carnatic Sultanate" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lemonjam · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nawab.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/state/carnatic-sultanate">State page: history, lineage and connections &rarr;</a></p>
